    "## Question 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08877903",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For question 1, we study how a consumer divides their fixed income between three goods: food, bus trips, and train trips. \n",
    "Bus and train are grouped together as a travel composite, which is then combined with food in a CES utility function. \n",
    "\n",
    "The goal is to find the budget shares that give the consumer the highest utility.\n",
    "\n",
    "We look at two cases: when bus and train are complements and when they are substitutes. We then compare the results to see how the budget shares change and how the consumer's utility is affected. We also check that the results satisfy the conditions of the model, meaning that all budget shares are strictly between 0 and 1 and that they sum to 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "047ceefb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
