   "source": [
    "### 5.1 Emissions with no taxes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ccbb2ae7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for name,green in greens.items():\n",
    "\n",
    "    eq = green.solve_with_rebate(np.zeros(3))\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(name)\n",
    "    print(f'  quantities = {np.round(eq.x,4)}')\n",
    "    print(f'  emissions  = {eq.E:.4f}')\n",
    "    print(f'  utility    = {eq.u:.4f}, welfare = {eq.W:.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d1196b59",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The substitutes consumer pollutes considerably more to begin with (0.339 against 0.239). Nothing green is going on: the bus is simply the cheaper of the two ways of travelling, and a consumer who is happy to substitute buys mostly the cheap one -- which here happens to be the dirty one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "408c3273",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.2 Two checks on the fixed point\n",
    "\n",
    "First, with the revenue rebated a tax at the *same* rate on all three goods must do nothing at all: it leaves every relative price unchanged and the rebate gives the lost income straight back. Second, preferences are homothetic, so the budget shares do not depend on income and the fixed point can be solved by hand: $R = I_{net}\\Phi$ with $\\Phi = \\sum_j \\frac{\\tau_j s_j}{1+\\tau_j}$ and $I_{net} = I+R$, so $R = I\\Phi/(1-\\Phi)$. The root-finder should agree with that."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ac1813d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for name,green in greens.items():\n",
    "\n",
    "    # a. neutrality of a uniform tax\n",
    "    eq0 = green.solve_with_rebate(np.zeros(3))\n",
    "    eq1 = green.solve_with_rebate(np.array([0.5,0.5,0.5]))\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(name)\n",
    "    print(f'  uniform tax : u = {eq1.u:.6f} vs {eq0.u:.6f}, E = {eq1.E:.6f} vs {eq0.E:.6f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "    # b. root-finder against the closed form\n",
    "    tau = np.array([0.0,0.3,0.05])\n",
    "    eq = green.solve_with_rebate(tau)\n",
    "    print(f'  rebate      : root-finder {eq.rebate:.8f}, closed form {green.rebate_closed_form(tau):.8f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "    assert np.isclose(eq1.u,eq0.u) and np.isclose(eq1.E,eq0.E), 'a uniform tax should be neutral'\n",
    "    assert np.isclose(eq.rebate,green.rebate_closed_form(tau)), 'the fixed point is wrong'\n",
    "\n",
